 @definingslawek4731  it’s not totally unusable, it’s nipping at the heals of the multi decade established market leaders in a lot of titles and is only falling badly short in titles where there’s clearly driver issues. They’ll overcome these issues with continued driver development. 

Release wise, Intel needed to get ARC out for 2 reasons. Waiting for perfection for a product with so many games it needs to run you’d never get it released. Better to have the cards out there and being used. Secondly it needed releasing in to the review cycle before the new gen cards imminently come out so it gets benched against current gen.

I’d potentially take a chance on one if I didn’t have a 3060Ti, I want more competition in the market so we minimise the chance of the last 2 years happening again.

